        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Additionally, I suggest changing this line:\n\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/4357160712c8e2c80318d46a827bf972fca24d61/lua/mini/extra.lua#L916\n\nto this:\n\n```\n      vim.schedule(function() vim.fn.feedkeys(id .. entry .. '\\r', 'nxt') end)\n```\n\nThe newly added \"t\" flag will cause the selected command to be newly recorded in the history, allowing it to be repeated using `@:` or `:<up><cr>`, which seems more natural\n\n---\n\nbefore:\n\n1. `:ls`\n2. `:smile`\n3. use the picker to choose `:ls`\n4. press `@:` -> execute `:smile`\n\nafter:\n\n1. `:ls`\n2. `:smile`\n3. use the picker to choose `:ls`\n4. press `@:` -> execute `:ls`",
